  "packageHashAlgorithm": "SHA512",
  "packageSize": 156285,
  "projectUrl": "https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard",
  "published": "2026-10-13T09:09:50.427Z",
  "readmeFile": "PackageReadme.md",
  "releaseNotes": "Requires exactly TokenGuard.Core 1.2.0, and Anthropic 12.53.0 or later. The package dependency on TokenGuard.Core is the exact version [1.2.0], so NuGet reports a mismatched Core version at restore.\n\nBehavior changes, with no signature changes: ForAnthropic() sends every text segment of a message as its own text block and every result of a tool message, where it used to send the first of each; it throws InvalidOperationException for a message it cannot represent, for unpaired tool calls and results, and for tool-call arguments that are not a JSON object. InputTokens() returns the total input of the request, including cache creation and cache read tokens, and null when the response carries no usage. From TokenGuard.Core 1.2.0: the default token budget is 40,000 instead of 25,000, and tool-result masking moves its boundary in steps.\n\nThis adapter is covered by unit tests only; no run against the Anthropic API has verified it. Known limits: summarization works with the built-in providers only, and a custom summarizer, compaction strategy, or token counter cannot be registered through the builder; one ConversationContext is for one caller at a time, and overlapping calls are detected on a best-effort basis; token estimates leave out request overhead such as tool schemas and undercount pretty-printed JSON by 17% to 30% until the first provider report; one tool result larger than the window cannot be fitted and the prepare returns CompactionInsufficient; the package targets net10.0 only.\n\nFull details: https://github.com/svetstoykov/TokenGuard/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md",
